            "review_title": "Review at Mùi Kitchen - Vietnamese Cuisine - Best Noodles!",
            "review_text": "Huy L\n1 contribution\n0\nSMELLS in Ho Chi Minh City !\nMar 2026 • Family\nI recently visited this restaurant because I heard it was newly opened. I was surprised after trying it out! 🤷‍♂️ The ambiance is amazing, and the food is only 30-55k VND per dish. We went with 5 people and ordered a set meal for 670k VND, and there was so much food! But I was wondering, why would a restaurant with such a beautiful space sell food and drinks so cheaply? 🤷‍♂️ After asking the owner, I found out that this restaurant was opened specifically for young people, students, etc. The staff are friendly and lovely. I'm sure you won't believe me if I say too much! You have to experience it for yourself to truly appreciate it. I rarely leave reviews, but because I'm so captivated by this place and its meticulous service, I'm making an exception so everyone can experience it for themselves. So there you go!!!\nRead more\nWritten March 30, 2026",
