            "review_text": "Kathy Ngo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam21 contributions\n0\nA true hidden gem of the city!\nMar 2026 • Family\nWent here with my family for dinner and had an amazing time. The architectural design was one of the most beautiful I've ever seen in a small cafe! They had a non-AC and air-conditioned floor. All decorated with beautiful Vietnamese traditional/modern fusion decor. We ordered their Set combo and a few à la carte items, a great deal for value. The portion was medium, but the taste was truly Vietnamese with a slightly sweet and salty taste. The owner said it was because the restaurant was Central-Vietnamese cuisine, hence the slightly saltier taste. Highly recommend their Fried rice with crab meat, their breakfast bowls. For à la carte items, Rolls with grilled meat, Chicken cartilage with pork cracklings were great. Took about 10 minutes for each dish. Try their homemade herbal drinks too, incredible aromatics. Definitely a must-visit if you're in District 7!\nRead more\nWritten March 30, 2026",
